      "path": "plugins/rotifer/cordis.patch.yml",
      "content": "# Rotifer bundle layer for DeepSeek Harness.\n#\n# Install (from this repository, not npm — the unscoped npm name `rotifer` is\n# held by a pointer package that exists to stop the toolchain being impersonated,\n# and this plugin has no bin to stand in for it):\n#   dsh plugin --profile <name> add \"github:rotifer-protocol/rotifer-playground#path:/plugins/rotifer\"\n#\n# Two rows, and both mount plugins DSH already ships. This bundle carries no\n# runtime code of its own, so a Cordis API change has nothing here to break.\n#\n# They appear in Settings -> Plugins as `rotifer-skills` and `rotifer-mcp`, not\n# as one entry named Rotifer: what a bundle contributes is rows, and these two\n# rows are configured instances of DSH's own skill provider and MCP bridge.\n# Both lead with the brand so one search for `rotifer` finds the whole set.\n# Override or disable either by that id from your own profile's cordis.patch.yml.\n\n- insert:\n    # The four Rotifer skills, from this package's own skills/ directory: the\n    # three skill folders plus the single-file rotifer-overview card, which this\n    # provider reads as a skill too (the other hosts read only the folders).\n    # includeDefaultRoots: false keeps this provider to that directory alone —\n    # it never rescans your project or user skill roots, so it cannot shadow a\n    # skill you wrote. The skills are read-only package files; nothing watches\n    # them for edits.\n    - id: rotifer-skills\n      name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-skill-filesystem'\n      config:\n        providerName: rotifer\n        includeDefaultRoots: false\n        watch: false\n        customSkillDirs:\n          - !!js \"process.getBuiltinModule('node:path').join(process.getBuiltinModule('node:module').createRequire(baseUrl).resolve('rotifer/package.json'), '..', 'skills')\"\n\n    # The Rotifer MCP server through DSH's own bridge, pinned to one version and\n    # narrowed to the evolve tool set: 10 tools, reaching Gene search, Arena\n    # rankings, install, rollback and local Agent runs. Left undeclared the\n    # server offers 31 tools, publish_gene, login and arena_submit among them,\n    # so this row is what keeps the assistant from publishing or signing in on\n    # your behalf. The launch line also omits --allow, so the sandbox escapes\n    # (no_sandbox, trust_unsigned) are refused.\n    #\n    # Cost: these 10 schemas are paid on EVERY request while the row is\n    # mounted — 6736 bytes of JSON, measured off ctx.tools.schemas() on\n    # dsh 0.1.0-rc.7. Remove this row and the four skills still work; they cost\n    # only their catalog rows.\n    #\n    # What it can change: installing a Gene writes to the project's genes/\n    # directory and always waits for your approval, the copy it replaces goes\n    # to genes/.snapshots/, and rollback_gene undoes it. Public Gene and Arena\n    # data needs no login, and login is not in this tool set. Usage reporting\n    # and the install counter are set out in the evolve skill's\n    # \"Security & Transparency\" section; ROTIFER_TELEMETRY=0 stops both.\n    - id: rotifer-mcp\n      name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-mcp-client'\n      config:\n        serverName: rotifer\n        transport: stdio\n        command: npx\n        args:\n          - '-y'\n          - '@rotifer/mcp-server@0.19.7'\n          - '--tools=evolve'\n        failOnStartupError: false\n"
